try><doc-number>11036920</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-11036926-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11036926</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-11287143-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11287143</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5288098-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>5288098</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUWA NAOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA MOTOR CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUWA, NAOHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA JIDOSHA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUWA NAOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUWA, NAOHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An engine which can be switched between a homogenous combustion mode and a stratified combustion mode and is controlled according to a load on the engine. During a homogenous combustion, an intake pressure, a parameter correlating with an intake air volume, is used as a value indicative of an engine load. During a stratified combustion, a value equivalent to an intake pressure at which a homogenous combustion is performed according to an operation amount of an acceleration pedal is calculated as a virtual intake pressure, the pressure being then used as a value indicative of an engine load.  In the both combustion modes, a common parameter, an intake pressure, is used as a value to indicate an engine load and control the engine, thereby simplifying a comparison between engine output torque characteristics in the two combustion modes.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur qui peut être commuté pour passer d'un mode de combustion homogène à un mode de combustion stratifié, et est contrôlé en fonction d'une charge sur le moteur. Pendant la combustion homogène, une pression d'admission, paramètre de corrélation avec un volume d'air d'admission, est utilisée comme valeur indiquant la charge du moteur. Pendant la combustion stratifiée, une valeur équivalente à une pression d'admission à laquelle une combustion homogène est assurée en fonction de la force d'accélération de la pédale d'accélateur, est calculée comme pression d'admission virtuelle et la pression sert alors de valeur indiquant la charge du moteur. Dans les deux modes de combustion, un paramètre commun, la pression d'admission, sert de valeur pour indiquer la charge du moteur et pour contrôler le moteur, ce qui simplifie la comparaison entre les caractéristiques de couple de sortie du moteur dans les deux modes de combustion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>